atility":0.043949464093205194,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":100.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.00729992367450202,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.02612320257178853,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.570817714249651,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":4.9,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.06110652232117386,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":13.0,"_gate_pool_share":-0.10864597041950841,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.008724341528293262,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":41.3,"_gate_fund_growth":0.028273551283954455,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":28.3,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0623385831444593,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":80.4,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.02727922180572051,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":84.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.006451375064513751,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":89.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.03846,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":25.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"BrightView Holdings, Inc., through its subsidiaries, provides commercial landscaping services in the United States. It operates in two segments, Maintenance Services and Development Services. The Maintenance Services segment delivers a suite of recurring commercial landscaping services, including mowing, gardening, mulching and snow removal, water management, irrigation maintenance, tree care, and golf course maintenance. Its customers' properties include corporate and commercial properties, homeowners associations, public parks, hotels and resorts, airport authorities, municipalities, hospitals and other healthcare facilities, educational institutions, restaurants and retail, and golf courses. The Development Services segment offers landscape architecture and development services for new facilities and redesign projects. This segment also provides project design and management services, landscape architecture and installation, irrigation installation, tree moving and installation, pool and water features, sports field, specialty turf maintenance, and other services. It operates as official field consultant to Major League Baseball. The company was formerly known as BrightView Acquisition Holdings, Inc. BrightView Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1939 and is headquartered in Blue Bell, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Dale A. Asplund | President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $2.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 16K people. Revenue per employee of $162K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["BrightView Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap industrials business with a $898M market cap on $2.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 4% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 24% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $40M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 1.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.2% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.8% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (35.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 59% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 56/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 38% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.6M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What BrightView Holdings (BV) Earnings Miss Means For Shareholders","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nyse-bv/brightview-holdings/news/what-brightview-holdings-bv-earnings-miss-means-for-sharehol","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794507682.477,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"JPMorgan Chase & Co. Has Lowered Expectations for BrightView (NYSE:BV) Stock Price","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/jpmorgan-chase-co-has-lowered-expectations-for-brightview-nysebv-stock-price.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794495038.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"748,393 Shares in BrightView Holdings, Inc. $BV Bought by Gagnon Securities LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/748393-shares-in-brightview-holdings-inc-bv-bought-by-gagnon-securities-llc.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794475884.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.935,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"BrightView (NYSE:BV) Share Price Breaks Below 50 Day Moving Average After Earnings Miss","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/brightview-nysebv-share-price-breaks-below-50-day-moving-average-after-earnings-miss.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794460852.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Brig